                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "[b]The game is so poorly designed it's unbeatable.[/b]\nIt's a picross game, so there is no excuse for how half-assed it is.\nThe interfase is clearly made for mobile, with the drag to change pages, I only noticed by accident. There is no support for the right mouse button (flagging button), instead you have to click a button to switch modes, making it as clunky as most of the UI. \nThere is also no restart button, you have to fail on purpose, then you can retry.\n\n[h1]Why the game can't be completed:[/h1]\nYou get 4 stars for completing stages without making a mistake. It requires replaying the stages because you lack information to get through it with logic.\nThe stars you get are not enough to unlock all levels, so [b]the game is unbeatable[/b]. I have every star I can collect, and I'm at 6 stars, unlocking any of the 70 levels I can't do, requires either 10 stars, for the official ones, or 4 stars for the \"community\" levels. I.e. they didn't even bother to check if the game could be beaten.\n\nSome you can cheese through by assuming that the image is symmetric, or in a particular pattern, but pretty much trial and error, particularly for the faux-minesweeper levels. \n\n[h1]The Minesweeper stages[/h1]\nThese levels are ill thought out. The number tells you if the amount of pixels to paint in the 9 pixel block that includes that numbers square. The reason minesweeper excludes the number's own square in the calculation is because that allows them to give you more information, not doing that means you can't diferentiate between neighboring squares really often. \nThis is compounded by the stupidest idea I've seen in a long time of making the \"clues\" (which numbers you can see) randomized each time you enter the stage. i.e. they only give you part of the information, most of the time, not enough to complete without having to guess your way through it, and then only letting you unlock more levels if you repeat it without mistakes.\nIf you want to try doing it, just bruteforce part of it, take a photo, and go on from there, and once you finish the level, repeat it following a photo of the completed puzzle.\n\nYou can get some extra stars by randomly completing \"collections\" of puzzles (no way to tell which levels are part of them) which build some scenes or drawings from some franchises like transformers, one piece, naruto and DBZ, but they aren't enough to unlock 10% of the levels I couldn't unlock despite having every star available.\n\n[h1]Conclusion[/h1]\nDon't waste your time. Picross can be a \"fun\" turn-off my brain for a minute kind of distraction while you do something else, but this implementation shows little effort, so in my opinnion, it isn't worth supporting.",
